</given-names></name><name><surname>Nurko</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Opioid side effects &#x02013; mechanism-based therapy</article-title><source>N Engl J Med</source><year>2008</year><volume>358</volume><fpage>2400</fpage><lpage>2402</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18509126</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1056/NEJMe0801783</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Liu</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Wittbrodt</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Low-dose oral naloxone reverses opioid-induced constipation and analgesia</article-title><source>J Pain Symptom Manage</source><year>2002</year><volume>23</volume><fpage>48</fpage><lpage>53</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11779668</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0885-3924(01)00369-4</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Liu</surname><given-names>SS</given-names></name><name><surname>Hodgson</surname><given-names>PS</given-names></name><name><surname>Carpenter</surname><given-names>RL</given-names></name><name><surname>Fricke</surname><given-names>JR</given-names><suffix>Jr</suffix></name></person-group><article-title>ADL 8-2698, a trans-3,4-dimethyl-4-(3-hydroxyphenyl) piperidine, prevents gastrointestinal effects of intravenous morphine without affecting analgesia</article-title><source>Clin Pharmacol Ther</source><year>2001</year><volume>69</volume><fpage>66</fpage><lpage>71</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11180040</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1067/mcp.2001.112680</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Spoel</surname><given-names>JI van der</given-names></name><name><surname>Schultz</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Voort</surname><given-names>PH van der</given-names></name><name><surname>de Jonge</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Influence of severity of illness, medication and selective decontamination on defecation</article-title><source>Intensive Care Med</source><year>2006</year><volume>32</volume><fpage>875</fpage><lpage>880</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16715327</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s00134-006-0175-9</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>